==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*bʰer-|*telh₂-|id2=bear}}
A {{glossary|suppletive}} paradigm consisting of two different roots.

The present stem is from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*ferō}} (infinitive {{m|itc-pro|*ferzi}}), from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*bʰéreti|t=to bear, carry}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|भरति|tr=bhárati}}, {{cog|fa|بار|tr=bâr}}, {{cog|xcl|բերեմ}}, {{cog|grc|φέρω}}, {{cog|ang|beran}} ({{cog|en|bear#Etymology_2}}).

The perfect stem, originally of {{m|la|tollō}}, is from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tetolai}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*tetólh₂e|t=to be holding up}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*telh₂-}}. The stem of {{m|la|lātus}} has the same root, reduced from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tlātos}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*tl̥h₂tós}}. It is cognate with {{cog|en|thole|t=to endure}}, {{cog|de|dulden|t=to endure}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|ferō}}

